## 🏇 Horse & Jockey Insights Page

Here's the complete Streamlit code snippet for your Horse & Jockey analytics page:

```python
import streamlit as st
import pandas as pd

# Placeholder Data (replace with real-time horse and jockey analytics retrieval)
horse_jockey_data = pd.DataFrame({
    "Horse": ["Lightning", "Thunder", "Storm", "Rain", "Sunshine"],
    "Jockey": ["John Doe", "Jane Smith", "Bob Johnson", "Alice Williams", "Chris Evans"],
    "Total Races": [25, 30, 15, 20, 18],
    "Wins": [10, 8, 6, 7, 9],
    "Win Rate (%)": [40, 26.7, 40, 35, 50]
})

# Page Title
st.title("🏇 Horse & Jockey Insights")

# Horse & Jockey Performance
st.subheader("Horse & Jockey Performance")
st.dataframe(horse_jockey_data, use_container_width=True)

# Win Rate Visualization
st.subheader("Win Rate (%) by Horse & Jockey")
st.bar_chart(horse_jockey_data.set_index("Horse")["Win Rate (%)"])

# Detailed Analysis (expandable)
for index, row in horse_jockey_data.iterrows():
    with st.expander(f"Details for {row['Horse']} - Jockey: {row['Jockey']}"):
        st.write(f"Total Races: {row['Total Races']}")
        st.write(f"Wins: {row['Wins']}")
        st.write(f"Win Rate (%): {row['Win Rate (%)']}")
```

